{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Craftsman.</b> He mentioned carved figures of stone and iron, and now also carved figures of wood." "<b>He stretches a line.</b> For thus is its rule." "<b>He shapes it.</b> He makes its form. The correct interpretation is that it is like ותאר לכם הגבל (Joshua 15:9), like the likeness of a tracing." "<b>In red ochre.</b> A type of coloring pigment, and there is nothing wrong with it [as a reading]." "<b>With tools.</b> He prepares. Rabbi Jonah of blessed memory says that the word hints at scoring [lines]." "<b>With a compass.</b> From the root חוג. It is the instrument with which one makes circles." "<b>In the beauty of a man.</b> Some say female, but there is no need; rather the phrase is doubled." "<b>To dwell in a house.</b> Like a person who sits in his house."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:58.527924018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}